  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for NRS_484B_410_o2, with 8 witnesses passing, and I used 2 of the 6 gate runs. My first run was a mistake: I ran it before writing anything, on the harness's skeleton files. I also piped it through `head`, so it wasn't the exact command you specified. It returned `UNUSED_CLAIM` and changed nothing; I've recorded it in `task_result.md`.\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_410_o2.lean`):\n- **Subject:** a member of the aggregate `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **Entry onto the highway:** the observation at which the subject first occupies a highway region (`.rises onHighway`).\n- **Exception:** at the observation before the entry, the subject was at rest and in one of two places. Either it occupied a curb zone that is no-parking, no-stopping or fire lane, or painted red. Or it occupied a travel region governed by a no-parking, no-standing or no-stopping sign whose conditions hold.\n- **How \"the observation before\" is written:** Core has no operator for \"at the previous observation\". So the applicability is `rises(onHighway) ∧ rises(onHighway ∨ haltedWhereNoParking)`. Because the first part makes the subject on the highway now, the second part says exactly that at the previous observation it was neither on a highway nor halted where no parking is permitted. The rule's header comment explains this.\n- **Obligation:** no other road user is predicted to come within `p.conflict_centre_clearance` of the subject within `p.conflict_horizon`.\n- **Narrowings:** none; every reading is the blueprint's.\n\n**The witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_410_o2.lean`):\n- **The four planned ones:**\n  - `forbid` is violated: the closest predicted approach is about 0.46 m, against the 3 m clearance.\n  - `permit` is compliant.\n  - `idle` is not applicable.\n  - `blind` is unknown, with `rel.occupies` masked.\n- **Four added branches**, one for each part of the exception:\n  - `branch_1`: halted in a fire lane → not applicable.\n  - `branch_2`: halted at a red curb → not applicable.\n  - `branch_3`: halted where a no-stopping sign applies → not applicable.\n  - `branch_4`: halted at an unrestricted white curb → violated.\n- **Window:** every witness judges only t = 1–3 s. At the first observation `rises` would read history from before the recording and report unknown.\n\nFiles are in `results/full221-1116-1018/iter-002/code/NRS_484B_410_o2/`:\n- task_result.md",
